.el .ds Aq '
.TH mdmc-pick-msgs 1  "msgs " 
.SH NAME
mdmc\-pick\-msgs \- Pick a message and print its message\-id
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmdmc pick msgs\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-folders\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-last\fR] [\fB\-\-multi\fR] [\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-page\-size\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pick a message and print its message\-id
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config.toml (default ~/.config/mdmc/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-folders\fR \fI<FOLDERS>\fR
Filter to these folders (comma\-separated: [folders] name, drafts, sent, or <account>.drafts/sent)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Restrict to messages whose sender matches this substring
.TP
\fB\-\-last\fR \fI<LAST>\fR
Only consider messages from the last N days (0 = no bound)
.TP
\fB\-\-multi\fR
Allow selecting multiple messages
.TP
\fB\-\-lines\fR
Print multiple selections one per line instead of comma\-separated
.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fI<PAGE_SIZE>\fR
Number of picker rows to show (default: [lookup] page_size)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
